(1) General inspection requirements:

(a) Notwithstanding any other provision of this chapter to the contrary, the director of the department of public works, or his designee, shall have the authority to inspect school buses where they are customarily housed or at inspection locations deemed appropriate by the director.

(b) Every school bus shall be painted National School Bus Glossy Yellow except that the hood shall be painted the same color or lusterless black and its roof may be painted white. Bumpers shall be painted glossy black, except that for increased night visibility they may be covered with a retroreflective material.

